Play: make Mesa's WGL frontend and d3d12 winsys usable inside a launcher guest (issue #176).
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT (same licence as the files patched; Mesa is MIT)

1. -DSTW_NO_DESKTOP_HOOKS (set by src/tools/build-mesa-d3d12.sh) selects Mesa's existing GDK-style code paths in the
   WGL frontend: no per-thread WH_CALLWNDPROC hook and thread snapshot, no EnumDisplaySettings/ClientToScreen, no
   wglUseFontOutlines GDI calls; window teardown is observed by subclassing the window procedure, resizes are
   polled at make-current/swap. A thread with no hook still gets its TLS record (upstream's GDK path would fail).
2. WGL target: without GALLIUM_DRIVER only the d3d12 driver is tried (no silent fall back to the CPU rasterizer,
   whose GDI blit has no surface under Play); GALLIUM_DRIVER=softpipe still selects it.
3. d3d12 WGL framebuffer: presents into a CoreWindow swapchain (Play's DXGI adapter maps the guest HWND to the app's
   CoreWindow): no ALLOW_TEARING or frame-latency-waitable flag, alpha ignored (no DirectComposition path), three
   flip buffers (Play creates at least three), Present never waits on a missing waitable object.

